# REPLIT AGENT BRIEF: EmotiLens, AI Product Feedback Intelligence System

## 1. APP OVERVIEW

**App name:** EmotiLens

**One-line description:** A web app where customers rate a product and write a review. A SimpleRNN deep-learning model detects the emotion, a separate sentiment classifier labels the review positive, negative or neutral, and a live dashboard turns the stored feedback into product insights.

**Core problem:** Star ratings do not explain *why* customers are happy or unhappy. Written reviews contain emotions, opinions and complaints, but they are unstructured and impossible to read at scale. EmotiLens converts raw feedback into organized, actionable analytics.

**Target user:**
- **Customers** submit a rating and a review.
- **Product and business teams** monitor satisfaction, emotions, trends and recurring complaints.

**Important honesty rules (apply everywhere in code, UI text and README):**
- The customer's star rating is always stored and shown separately from AI output. The AI never replaces or overrides the rating.
- The emotion model is trained on the general `dair-ai/emotion` dataset, not product reviews. State this limitation in the UI.
- Never hardcode or claim an accuracy figure. Show only metrics computed by the evaluation script on the test set.
- Sentiment comes from a separate component (VADER), not from the 6-class emotion model. Do not describe the emotion model as a validated 3-class sentiment classifier.
- Issue grouping is keyword-based and lightweight. Label it "Keyword-based issue detection".

