## 6. DATA & APIS

### Data models

**products**
| Field | Type |
|---|---|
| id | Integer, primary key |
| name | String(120), unique |
| description | Text |
| emoji | String(8) |

**feedback**
| Field | Type |
|---|---|
| feedback_id | Integer, primary key |
| product_id | FK → products.id, indexed |
| rating | Integer (1–5, check constraint) |
| feedback_text | Text |
| predicted_emotion | String(20) |
| emotion_probabilities | JSON (dict of 6 emotion→probability) |
| sentiment | String(10): positive / negative / neutral |
| sentiment_score | Float (VADER compound, −1 to 1) |
| confidence_score | Float (top emotion probability) |
| mismatch_flag | Boolean |
| issue_categories | JSON (list of strings) |
| created_at | DateTime, default now, indexed |

### Label mapping
Load the label names from the dataset itself (`dataset["train"].features["label"].names`) and save them to `ml/artifacts/labels.json`. The expected order is `["sadness", "joy", "love", "anger", "fear", "surprise"]`. Always use the saved file at inference time, not a hardcoded list.

### Sentiment logic (`services/sentiment.py`)
- Use VADER `SentimentIntensityAnalyzer`. Compound ≥ 0.05 → positive; ≤ −0.05 → negative; otherwise neutral.
- Return the label and the compound score.

### Mismatch logic
- `mismatch_flag = True` if (rating ≥ 4 and sentiment == "negative") or (rating ≤ 2 and sentiment == "positive").

### Issue keyword dictionary (`services/issues.py`)
Apply only to feedback where sentiment == "negative" or rating ≤ 2. Match lowercase substrings and word stems:
- **Battery:** battery, charge, charging, drain
- **Performance:** slow, lag, laggy, freeze, freezes, performance, loading
- **Crashes / Bugs:** crash, crashes, crashing, bug, bugs, error, glitch, broken
- **Price:** expensive, overpriced, price, cost, waste of money
- **Shipping / Delivery:** shipping, delivery, delayed, late, arrived damaged, packaging
- **Customer support:** support, customer service, refund, no response, waiting
- **Quality / Durability:** cheap, flimsy, broke, defective, poor quality, stopped working
- **UI / Usability:** confusing, hard to use, interface, clunky, navigation

A review can match multiple categories.

### Text preprocessing (`ml/preprocess.py`)
- Lowercase, strip, collapse whitespace, remove URLs and HTML tags, keep letters, digits, apostrophes and basic punctuation, then split on whitespace.
- Use identical preprocessing at training and inference time.

### API endpoints (all JSON, prefix `/api`)
| Method & path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `GET /api/health` | `{status, model_loaded}` |
| `GET /api/products` | Products with `avg_rating`, `review_count`, `top_emotion` |
| `POST /api/feedback` | Body `{product_id, rating, feedback_text}`. Validate (rating 1–5, text 5–1000 chars). Run the pipeline, save, and return the saved record plus the full emotion probabilities. |
| `POST /api/analyze` | Body `{text}`. Return emotion, probabilities, sentiment and score. Do not save. |
| `GET /api/feedback` | Query params: `product_id, sentiment, emotion, rating, q, sort, page, page_size`. Return `{items, total, page, pages}`. |
| `GET /api/feedback/export` | CSV download with the same filters. |
| `GET /api/analytics/summary` | Query: `product_id?, days?`. Return KPIs (avg rating, total, sentiment percentages, top emotion, mismatch count) and the rule-based insight text. |
| `GET /api/analytics/emotions` | Emotion counts and percentages. |
| `GET /api/analytics/ratings` | Count per star level. |
| `GET /api/analytics/trends` | Daily series (or weekly when days > 60): avg rating, review count, positive count, negative count. |
| `GET /api/analytics/issues` | Ranked issue categories with counts and up to 2 example snippets. |
| `GET /api/analytics/emotion-rating-matrix` | 6×5 count matrix. |
| `GET /api/model/metrics` | Contents of `ml/artifacts/metrics.json`, or a `{available:false}` payload. |

No external third-party APIs are required. Everything runs locally. The only external downloads are the Hugging Face dataset (once, during training) and the CDN assets (Chart.js, Google Fonts).

